# CMake build tree for the C++ oracle. Configured with:
#   cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5
build/

# The ooTest conformance suite, checked out from SVN by Phase 0.
ootest/

# The ooRexx documentation, DocBook XML from the same SVN repository as
# ootest/ (^/docs/trunk, where ootest/ is ^/test/trunk). Checked out
# 2026-08-17 because the object model is documented here and nowhere in the
# C++ tree: rexxref/en-US/fundclasses.xml is the fundamental-class reference
# and rexxpg/en-US/classes.xml is the Programming Guide's object-model
# chapter. Only those two books are checked out; the rest of ^/docs/trunk is
# other products.
#   svn checkout https://svn.code.sf.net/p/oorexx/code-0/docs/trunk/rexxref oodocs/rexxref
#   svn checkout https://svn.code.sf.net/p/oorexx/code-0/docs/trunk/rexxpg  oodocs/rexxpg
oodocs/

# Extracted L1 micro-programs: 12,059 files / 49 MB, regenerated by
#   cargo run -p rexx-extract --bin rexx-extract -- \
#       --suite ootest --out rust/corpus-l1 --report docs/superpowers/plans/l1-coverage.md
#
# Deliberately a sibling of rust/corpus/, not a child. rexx-diff walks its
# --corpus argument recursively, so nesting the 12,059 L1 programs inside the
# 13-program L0 corpus turned the Phase 0 self-test into 24,000 interpreter
# invocations and a two-minute timeout.
rust/corpus-l1/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledgers, briefs, review packages.
.superpowers/
